      "math_academy_id": "e-14655",
      "problem": "Is the following statement true or false?\n\nThe integer $21$ is the additive inverse of $14$ modulo $35.$",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $14$ modulo $35$ is the integer $0 \\leq x \\lt 35$ such that\n\n$$\nx + 14 \\equiv 0 \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\:35).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is congruent to zero modulo $35{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21+14 & ≡35 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the statement is true.",
